Rule 139: an empty table keeps its
header. The header reads `Images: <visible rows>`, the title carries the typed
name (`... > Registry Browser > <name>`) at level 1 (once `→` opens a row, the
title carries that row's name, see below), and the footer shows the shared
activity dot with `Searching registries...` while `pendingSearches > 0`. Once
new generation and zeroes `pendingSearches`, so a late tag answer or failure is
dropped by the generation test and cannot show `Could not load tags` over the
form or level 1 (this closes open point 5 of D132). It also resets the tag
filters (`registryFilter`, `filterInput`, `filterActive`) and `tagsImage`, so
the title does not keep a stale `[alias]` or image name. Level 1 itself:
`←` goes back to the form (`backToForm`, which also calls `abandonLot`) and
keeps the typed name and the selected registries, even with a confirmed filter
query. `esc` still clears a confirmed query first. While the filter bar is being
typed in, `esc` closes the bar and `←` stays in the text field. There is no `←`
entry in the shortcuts header: `esc Go back` already shows in both states
(Rule 130, D133).

**Networks, Volumes and Registries (DEVDESK-153, A-09b).** Each takes
`datatable.IndicatorColumn` as column 0. Rows carry no `components.RowActivity`:
the datatable reads its own busy marker (`MarkBusy`), and the column's
`Indicator` function returns `Idle` (or `Running` when `registryRow.refreshing`
the other way: four cumulative tokens the table owns, and its sort and its
search are the table's too. The
registry browser is the third: its text filter and its registry filter narrow
the tags *before* the table sees them, and its bar is drawn in the OCI view's
own footer rather than the table's. Its **sort** is the table's — `.` cycles
Tag and Updated through `CycleSort`, and `SetSort` is what puts a new search
back on the default order.

The browser's **search form** has one `enter` entry in the header
(Rule 130), whose label follows the focus (`RegistryBrowser.FormEnter()`):
`Search` on Repository and on the Search button, `Open tags` on the Open Tags
button, `Browse tags` where no `Searcher` is wired. It is lit on Repository and
on a button, greyed on a checkbox (there `enter` only moves the focus). The
buttons come from `formButtons()`, the same list the keyboard and the rendering
read (`network.md`); the help text follows the mode (`registryBrowserHelpBody`).

The browser's **level 1** (image search results, `searchTable`) is the
opposite case: it uses the `datatable` filter bar as is (Rule 136). `/` opens it
and filters on Name and Description; the bar is drawn in the OCI view's footer
through `FilterBarView`, and its height counts through `FilterIsVisible`. `esc`
acts in order: it closes the bar while it is being typed in (the bar takes the
key), then clears a confirmed query (`ClearSearch`, level 1 stays), then
cancels the lot in flight (late answers are ignored) and goes back to the
search form, which keeps the typed name and the selection. The plan had `esc`
go back without cancelling; cancelling was chosen and recorded in D129.
`←` goes back to the form at once, even with a confirmed query (it is not
cleared), and keeps the typed name and the selection; while the bar is typed in,
`←` stays in the text field. On tags opened by `→`, `←` and `esc` return to
level 1 with the same cursor, sort and filter and no new request; on tags opened
by full name they return to the form (`network.md`, DEVDESK-307).
`→` opens the tags of the row under the cursor (`network.md`, DEVDESK-304); with
no row it warns `No image selected` in the footer and its shortcut is greyed
(`imageDrillIn`, the same computation for the header and the handler). `enter`
does nothing at level 1 (a row has no action yet) and is not in the shortcuts.
The set of keys does not depend on the rows (Rule 130): `→ Open tags` (greyed
without a row), `. Sort` (cycles Name, Registry, Stars, then the default order; `network.md`, DEVDESK-309), `/ Filter` and `esc Go back` (no `←` entry: it does the same
as `esc`; `←` is named only in the `?` help), or `enter/esc Close filter` while
typing. The `?` help lists `. (Browser images)`. A new search resets the sort and the confirmed filter. The title carries the typed name, or the opened row's name once `→` has
opened its tags.

`status` is the two-table case: two `datatable.Model` plus a focus helper.

